// Title: BITTER / PapRAT - ftp.exe local command shell child
// Rule name: T1059.003 - ftp.exe local command shell child
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR advanced hunting
// Telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint DeviceProcessEvents
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.003 - Windows Command Shell
// Purpose: Identify cmd.exe process creation with the native Windows FTP client as its direct initiating process.
// Logic: Two documented process-name equality filters; the portal time picker controls the search interval.
// Match proves: Defender XDR recorded cmd.exe with InitiatingProcessFileName represented as ftp.exe.
// Match does not prove: use of the FTP ! token, malicious script content, LNK execution, scheduled-task creation,
// PapRAT deployment, C2, reconnaissance, exfiltration, compromise, or BITTER attribution.
// False positives: authorized legacy FTP automation using !, compatibility/security testing, or lineage-quality issues.
// Limits: DeviceProcessEvents does not guarantee visibility into the FTP script token or file contents; the exact
// parent-child representation and target-environment prevalence have not been validated.
// Validation: run the controlled positive and negative tests in validation.md before any alert promotion.
// Evidence claims: C002, C004, C005, C006, C007, C008, C009

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName =~ "cmd.exe"
| where InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "ftp.exe"
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceId,
    DeviceName,
    AccountName,
    InitiatingProcessAccountName,
    FileName,
    FolderPath,
    ProcessCommandLine,
    SHA1,
    ProcessUniqueId,
    InitiatingProcessFileName,
    InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
    InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    InitiatingProcessSHA1,
    InitiatingProcessUniqueId,
    InitiatingProcessParentFileName,
    ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
